{"text": "Netto, Ellen\nWednesday, February 07. 2001 5:21 PM\nMcCormick, Brendan J.; Murphy, Virginia; Grant, Ellen; Brickell, Julia\nEulo, Maria: Pfeil, Michael E,\nRE: Draft statement for use re: RUR\n\nagain, i would change the emphasis. start with the \"Nothing in pmusa merch program... then follow with sentence\n\u2018about dynamic, highly competive nature and finally end with your frst sentence about how we compete.\n\nOriginal Message\u2014\nFrom: McCormick, Brendan J,\nSent: Wednesday, February 07, 2001 6:14 PM\nTo: Murphy, Virginia: Grant, Ellen; Brickel, Julia; Meso, Ellen\nCe: Eulo, Maria; Proll, Michaol E\nSubject: Draft statement for use re: RR\n\nBelow is a draft statement for use if RIR goes to cout in the Retail Leaders suit. Please review and let me know if you\nhave any comments.\n\nDRAFT FOR DISCUSSION\n\u2018Statement fr use in response to calls if RJR goes to court on retail issues:\n\nPhilip Mortis USA competes vigorously in tne marketplace and is confident that its retail merchandising programs are in\nfull compliance with the cous order and the law.\n\nTobacco company merchandising programs have changed a numberof times since June 1999, reflecting the dynamic,\nhighly competitive nature of the market. Nothing in Philip Mortis USA's merchandising program, now or since the\nInception ofthis suit, has precluded RJR or any other cigarette manufacturer from promoting its brands. RJR has.\napparently been able to compete and promote successfully, as reflected in the recent launch of its Camel Turkish Gold\nbrand.\n\nIf asked about the status of the original lawsuit:\nIn March 1988, RJ Reynolds fled sult against Philip Morris USA, complaining about Philip Mortis USA's Retail Leaders\n\n\u2018program. In June 1999, the Court entered an order calling or limited changes to one level of the Retailer Leaders.\n\u2018program, pending tial on the merits. The trial isin the discovery phase and depositions are being taken, No trial date\nhas been set\n\nPhilip Morris USA continues to believe that, inthe final analysis, PM's program will be found to be completely lawful\nPhilip Mortis USA competes vigorously and in compliance with all applicable laws, and our retail merchandising program\nis no exception,\n\n2712600297",
